  "source": "Rish LM 1340 and LM 1360+ Interface Definitions",
  "notes": [
    "Rish LM1350 / LM1360 load managers.",
    "Each measured value is a float32 (IEEE 754, most significant byte first) in two registers, readable as 3X input registers with FC04 and as 4X holding registers with FC03 at the same addresses (30001 / 40001 = address 0). At most 40 parameters per request.",
    "There is no interface definition for the LM1350 or LM1360 themselves: the table is the one shared by the LM1340 and LM1360+ documents, which list the same first parameters. Parameters beyond the first 51 are not in this map.",
    "Not tested on a device."
  ],
